// The Community rules (decision #122), shown on every Community page so they are never out of sight.
---
<section class="card stack" aria-labelledby="c-rules">
  <h2 id="c-rules">Our rules for this work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>History and culture only.</strong> No clan counts or rankings, and nothing tied to elections or land claims.</li>
    <li><strong>Every account names its source:</strong> a book, an archive, or an elder who agreed to be recorded.</li>
    <li><strong>Several voices.</strong> Where accounts differ, we show each one.</li>
    <li><strong>Checked before publishing</strong> by a review panel of elders and a historian.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent, on record.</strong> Every contributor agrees to how their words are used, and can withdraw. Using a recording to train language technology needs its own, separate yes.</li>
    <li><strong>The community keeps the rights.</strong> Contributors are credited unless they ask not to be, and are paid or thanked for their time.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
